{"name":"Adriatic Sea","hex":"#016081","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Adriatic Sea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A sea and arm of the Mediterranean Sea, stretching north from the Ionian Sea to Venice, separating the Italian and Balkan Peninsulas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Adriatic_Sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adriatic Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Adriatic Sea is a body of water separating the Italian Peninsula from the Balkan Peninsula. The Adriatic is the northernmost arm of the Mediterranean Sea, extending from the Strait of Otranto to the northwest and the Po Valley. The countries with coasts on the Adriatic are Albania, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, Italy, Montenegro, and Slovenia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Adriatic_Sea_2003.jpg/330px-Adriatic_Sea_2003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adriatic_Sea","wikidata":"Q13924"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Bucht_von_Kotor.jpg/500px-Bucht_von_Kotor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Bucht_von_Kotor.jpg/1280px-Bucht_von_Kotor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse